// The rendered counterpart of cameras.json5: the same wrist camera and the
// same instance id, so a simulated session records the dataset image key a
// real one does (observation.images.wrist). The frames come from the
// simulation, so there is no device path and no udev rule here; the relay
// pairs into the simulation's rgb_cameras slot and presents the rgb_camera
// contract exactly as the uvc node does, and describes its device through
// camera_profile, which the uvc node does not. The slot holds any number of pairs: the simulation tells
// a pair's robot by its copy and its camera by the relay's name in that
// copy, the instance id written here.
//
// The relay also holds a control slot for the simulation's camera response
// model (sim_camera_control), which forwards the controls a consumer sets
// on the camera to the simulation's model of that camera. Waldo implements
// it, so the relay binds it there; MuJoCo and Isaac Sim have no response
// model, so the slot is written vacant and every camera control refuses on
// them.
//
// The launcher binds the rig to the recorder, the headset and, under the
// MCP commander, the stack's MCP endpoint, the rendered relay listed with
// its profile and geometry. The browser scene
// commander's camera panel reads the cameras from the simulation, which
// lists every robot's, so the rig links nothing else into the stack.
//
// Camera placement, intrinsics and rate live with the simulation, in its
// so101 model.
{
  peppy_schema: "launcher_fragment/v1",

  deployments: [
    {
      // The wrist camera: the simulation renders the view from the gripper
      // and the relay republishes it.
      source: { name: "sim_rgb_camera", tag: "v1" },
      instances: [
        { instance_id: "wrist",
          links: {
            simulation: "simulation_inst/rgb_cameras",
            control: { vacant: "this simulation has no camera response model; every camera control refuses" },
          },
          framework: { clock: "simulation" } },
      ],
    },
  ],

  adjustments: [
    // Waldo models the rendered camera's response after the real device,
    // so the relay forwards its controls to it.
    { target: "wrist", when: { simulation: "waldo" }, set_links: { control: "simulation_inst" } },
  ],
}
